{"name":"Sparkling Lavender","hex":"#eeccff","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sparkling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of sparkle"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, reflecting light as if giving off tiny sparks or flashes of light.","Of a beverage, especially an alcoholic beverage, containing dissolved carbon dioxide (either naturally or that has been added) that comes out of solution in the form of many tiny bubbles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sparkling"},{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sparkling","blocks":[{"text":"Sparkling is an optical phenomenon exhibited by materials, both solids and liquids, in which numerous points of light appear and disappear, or change in brightness as the material, observer, or light source moves, creating an impression of brilliance and visual movement. In many materials, this effect results from specular reflection by small reflective particles, facets, or flakes that direct incident light toward the observer, although sparkling can also result from refraction and other optical phenomena."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Preferential_concentration.gif/330px-Preferential_concentration.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sparkling"},{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the 